course: dictionary
lesson: 15272
title: A big word for meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Signification is a long, formal word for meaning. You will mostly find it in old books, in language study, and in philosophy, which is the study of big ideas. In everyday talk, people just say «meaning».
explain: Signification can mean the meaning of a word, sign or symbol. «The signification of a word» is what that word stands for. Signification can also mean the act of showing or signalling something, like a nod that says yes.
explain: When you meet signification, swap in the word meaning and check the sentence. «The signification of this red sign is stop» still makes sense with meaning, so you have understood it.
fact: Signification is a noun. Its plural is significations.
fact: Signification means the meaning of a word, sign or symbol.
fact: Signification can also mean the act of showing or signalling something.
fact: «The signification of a word» means what the word stands for.
fact: It is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in old books and language study. In everyday talk, use «meaning».
exercise: «The signification of this road sign is no parking.» What does signification mean here? | *The meaning of the sign | The size of the sign | The price of the sign | The colour of the sign
exercise: «The teacher's raised hand had a clear signification: be quiet.» What does signification mean here? | A type of hand | A kind of paint | The name of a teacher | *The act of signalling something
exercise: Which everyday word can you use instead of signification in «the signification of a word»? | *meaning | length | colour | shape
test: «The true signification of this old word was lost over time.» What does signification mean here? | The price | *The meaning | The spelling | The number of letters
test: Which everyday word is closest in meaning to signification? | colour | *meaning | sound | weight
exam: «Ben's wave gave a clear signification that he was leaving.» In this sentence, signification means what? | a long word | *the act of signalling something | a loud noise | a type of bird
